WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.350
- [Narrator] This is the eastern
Ukrainian City of Bakhmut

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.270
in summer 2022,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.770
and this is what it looked
like half a year later.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.290
Moscow has been trying to
take Bakhmut since last July,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.360
turning it into the sight
of the bloodiest fight

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.863
of Russia's war in Ukraine.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.520
While some military analysts
and Western officials

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.350
have debated how important the city is

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.410
to the overall conflict,
both Moscow and Kyiv

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.911
have doubled down on
their military operations.

00:00:27.911 --> 00:00:31.411
(Sergei speaking Russian)

00:00:34.014 --> 00:00:37.931
(Volodymyr speaking Ukrainian)

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.320
- [Narrator] Here's how Bakhmut turned

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.750
into a political symbol
for Kyiv and Moscow

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.600
and why this battle has been
so difficult for both sides.

00:00:47.371 --> 00:00:49.020
(upbeat music)

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.720
Located in the highly
contested Donetsk region,

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.850
Bakhmut wasn't an obvious spot on the map

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.430
to become one of the
focal points of the war.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.860
The city does sit on a
number of major roads,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.080
linking it to strategically
important locations

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:01.913
in the region.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.210
But Bakhmut itself isn't a
significant transportation hub

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.430
according to some military analysts,

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.010
and the city's hilly terrain
makes it a difficult place

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.000
to advance from.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.430
- If the Russians do
eventually take Bakhmut,

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.843
they'll have to go over higher ground

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.930
and the Ukrainians have had plenty of time

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.483
to build highly defensible
positions there.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:23.910
- [Narrator] Some of those positions

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.470
are in the town of Chasiv Yar

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.050
that sits on a hill around six miles west

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.300
where Ukrainians have
been digging trenches.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.930
More can be found further west
in Kramatorsk and Slovyansk,

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.020
the heavily fortified Ukrainian
strongholds in Donetsk.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:37.853
- [Stephen] It's not gonna be easy

00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:40.863
for the Russians from now on
even if they take the the city.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.160
- [Narrator] This makes it
unlikely that taking control

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.770
of the city would be a
turning point for Russia.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.729
So why have both sides
continued to fight for the city?

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:51.630
Ukrainian commanders say they aim

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.480
to exhaust Russian forces
there and give themselves time

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.880
to prepare for offensives of their own,

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.740
and for Russia, the battle has turned

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.900
into a defining moment for Wagner,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.570
the mercenary group that
spearheaded the Russian offensive.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.060
Thanks to them, the region
surrounding the city

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.260
is one of the few places

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.130
where Moscow has made any major
progress since last summer.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.030
But to do this,

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.270
the group has invested almost
its entire supply of recruits,

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.943
sending waves of soldiers
to near certain death.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.690
In March, a UK military advisor estimated

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.840
that between 20,000 and
30,000 Russian troops

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.050
have been killed or wounded
in the area around Bakhmut

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.880
since the start of the offensive.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.570
- Bakhmut has developed a
symbolic significance far greater

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:38.374
than the operational or strategic
significance of the city.

00:02:38.374 --> 00:02:41.130
- [Narrator] And military
analysts say Ukraine's losses,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.800
which are classified, are also increasing.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.309
Russian and Ukrainian military
officials didn't respond

00:02:46.309 --> 00:02:47.820
to our request for comment

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.546
on the number of casualties
they've suffered in Bakhmut.

00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:52.230
(upbeat music)

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.270
Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.830
has come under criticism at home

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.010
for deciding to defend Fortress
Bakhmut as he called it,

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.513
despite mounting deaths.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.200
But in late March, Western officials

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.500
and some military analysts
said Russia's offensive

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.820
in Bakhmut was losing momentum.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.130
- It may be that the Russians

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.020
have effectively exhausted themselves

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.020
or it may be that the
Russians are just pausing,

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:21.020
hoping to resupply and go at
it again with one final push.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:23.760
- [Narrator] Despite questions about

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.680
the city's strategic importance,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.720
the large number of troops and ammunition

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.000
that both sides have
poured into the battle

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.910
has created a military
significance of its own.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.340
- The next thing really to watch

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.340
will be what happens when
Ukrainian forces re-equipped

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.760
with Western tanks and other
sophisticated equipment

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.633
and try to take back more
land occupied by the Russians.

